    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "ASSERTIONS AND LOGGING\n\nAssert nodes turn assumptions into checks: Assert True, Assert Equals, Assert Eq Int, Assert Lt Int ...\nA failed assertion stops the script and names the node, which makes them the quickest way to test a\nBlueprint. Logging nodes (info / warn / error) write to the engine log at a severity so you can filter\nthem, and Conditional Print only speaks when its condition is true. This graph passes every check.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          210.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "ASSERT\nAssert True, then 2 + 2 is wired into Assert Eq Int(actual) and compared with the typed-in expected value 4. Assert Equals compares two strings; Lt Int / Ne Int compare numbers.",
        "position": [
          360.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1760.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
